            <ArticleTitle>Intrauterine devices: insertion and removal: practical procedures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Intrauterine devices (IUDs) remain a popular and common method of contraception in Australia. Their insertion and removal are commonplace in general practice. Dr Ken Waldron believes the success of the IUD depends, in part, on observing correct insertion techniques.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
